<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rüdesheim am Rhein</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Rüdesheim</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rüdesheim am Rhein is a wine town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> at the start of the Rhine Gorge, part of the Upper Middle Rhine Valley World Heritage Site. Famous for its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/riesling">Riesling</a> vineyards, it lies below the Niederwald Monument, built in 1877–1883 to commemorate the founding of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rudesheim-am-rhein.jpg" alt="Rüdesheim am Rhein" width="320" height="120" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: DXR · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Panoramic_View_of_R%C3%BCdesheim_am_Rhein_20140928_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
